# ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
# │  FileShift — environment configuration                               │
# │                                                                       │
# │  Single file used by BOTH deployment modes:                          │
# │    • Docker:  docker-compose reads this for ${VAR} substitution      │
# │    • Local:   backend/src/config loads it via dotenv                 │
# │                                                                       │
# │  1.  Copy to .env:    cp .env.example .env                           │
# │  2.  Set DOWNLOAD_TOKEN_SECRET (instructions below)                  │
# │  3.  Done — the app refuses to start without it in production.       │
# ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯


# ─── REQUIRED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# HMAC signing secret for download tokens. Must be a strong random string.
# The same secret must be used by the API and the worker, which is why we
# put it here (one file, both services).
#
# Generate one:
#   Linux/macOS:  openssl rand -hex 32
#   Windows PS:   -join ((1..64) | % { '{0:x}' -f (Get-Random -Max 16) })
#
# IMPORTANT: rotating this invalidates every issued download token.
# DOWNLOAD_TOKEN_SECRET= Add-Content .env "`nDOWNLOAD_TOKEN_SECRET=$(-join ((1..64) | % { '{0:x}' -f (Get-Random -Max 16) }))"


# ─── SHARED (used by both Docker and local dev) ────────────────────────────

# CORS allow-list for the API.
#   Docker compose default frontend port:  http://localhost:8080
#   Local Vite dev server:                 http://localhost:5173
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080

# Hard upload limit, enforced by multer. Default 500 MB.
MAX_FILE_SIZE=524288000

# Files older than this get deleted by the cleanup cron.
RETENTION_HOURS=2

# How often the cleanup cron runs.
CLEANUP_INTERVAL_MINUTES=15

# Per-job hard timeout. After this, the conversion is SIGKILLed.
JOB_TIMEOUT_MS=600000

# Retry count on transient failure.
JOB_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2

# Parallel jobs PER worker process. With multiple workers, total
# concurrency = WORKER_CONCURRENCY × number of worker containers.
WORKER_CONCURRENCY=2

# Download token lifetime in seconds. Should be ≤ RETENTION_HOURS so tokens
# don't outlive the files they reference.
DOWNLOAD_TOKEN_TTL=3600


# ─── DOCKER ONLY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public-facing port for the nginx frontend container.
# Visit http://localhost:<FRONTEND_PORT>/
FRONTEND_PORT=8080


# ─── LOCAL DEV ONLY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are ignored when running via docker-compose (compose sets its own
# values that point at the redis service name on the docker network).

# Where the backend API listens.
PORT=4000

# 'development' enables friendlier error messages and disables the
# DOWNLOAD_TOKEN_SECRET safety check. Set to 'production' for real deploys.
NODE_ENV=development

# Redis connection. With docker-compose, REDIS_HOST=redis (the service name).
# For local dev, point at wherever your Redis is running.
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379
# REDIS_PASSWORD=    # uncomment if your Redis requires AUTH


# ─── CONVERSION TOOL PATHS (local dev only — Docker has them on PATH) ──────
# Leave empty if the tools are on PATH. Set explicitly only when auto-detect
# can't find them. On Windows, LibreOffice almost always needs this set.

# IMAGEMAGICK_PATH=
# FFMPEG_PATH=
# LIBREOFFICE_PATH=C:\Program Files\LibreOffice\program\soffice.exe
